{"id": "fh-0069", "domain": "standup flow", "names": ["Yesterday", "Today", "Blockers", "Ask", "Done"], "text": "Okay I'm sketching our standup flow, it's a mess right now. Yesterday goes to Today, and Today goes to Blockers. If there are blockers, they go to Ask. Make Ask orange, that's our warning color. Is Ask connected to Yesterday? Hmm, probably not, I want to double check. Which shape is the most connected? Rename Blockers to Risks, the product people like that word better. After that, put Done at the bottom right. And connect Ask to Done, because a question gets answered eventually. Undo that last connection, it's wrong. Also list all the orange shapes. Thanks, this helps a lot.", "wires": [{"span": "Yesterday goes to Today, and Today goes to Blockers", "trigger": "goes to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Yesterday,Today,Blockers", "pairing": "chain"}}, {"span": "they go to Ask", "trigger": "go to", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Blockers", "to": "Ask"}}, {"span": "Make Ask orange", "trigger": "Make", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "set", "target": "Ask", "color": "orange"}}, {"span": "Is Ask connected to Yesterday", "trigger": "Is Ask connected to", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "connected", "target": "Ask", "anchor": "Yesterday"}}, {"span": "Which shape is the most connected", "trigger": "most connected", "type": "question", "args": {"ask": "extreme", "superlative": "mostConnected"}}, {"span": "Rename Blockers to Risks", "trigger": "Rename", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "rename", "target": "Blockers", "name": "Risks"}}, {"span": "put Done at the bottom right", "trigger": "put", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "move", "target": "Done", "position": "bottomRight"}}, {"span": "connect Ask to Done", "trigger": "connect", "type": "command", "args": {"action": "connect", "from": "Ask", "to": "Done"}}, {"span": "Undo that last connection", "trigger": "Undo", "type": "command", "args":